---
import Layout from '../layouts/StaticPage.astro';

import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../consts';
---

<Layout
	title="Working with Mike Susz: front-end, design systems, accessibility"
	description="What it's like to bring me onboard."
>
	<section id="introduction" aria-label="Introduction">
		<p>
			In 30 years of work I've joined many teams, and there's a pattern to making both an initial
			and a lasting impact. In a nod to the 30/60/90-day format of many of the job descriptions I've
			seen – here's what it will be like to bring me onboard.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- first 30 days -->

	<section id="first30" aria-label="First 30 Days">
		<h2>First 30 days: Observe, absorb</h2>

		<p>
			I listen more than I speak. I get to know the team, the codebase, and the people everything
			quietly depends on, and I learn which processes everyone actually follows and which are
			aspirational.
		</p>

		<p>
			Beyond ramping-up, I like to deliver a quick win – identify and relieve a pain point that the
			team may or may not even have known they had. I want everyone to be better off on day 30 than
			they were on day 0.
		</p>
	</section>

	<!-- 30 - 60 days -->
	<section id="30-to-90" aria-label="30 to 90 Days">
		<h2>30 to 90 days: Adapt, suggest, improve</h2>

		<p>
			I start to make small, low-risk improvements. I set an example of engineering discipline –
			atomic commits, documentation, communication, and testing. We begin addressing the pain points
			I've observed.
		</p>

		<p>
			I also use my 'new guy' perspective to ask difficult questions on behalf of the team –
			addressing technical debt, fixing broken or tedious workflows, considering things like
			maintainability and accessibility that sometimes get overlooked when under timeline pressure.
		</p>

		<!-- 90 days + -->
		<section id="90-plus" aria-label="90 plus days">
			<h2>90+ Days: Lead, support, reflect, iterate</h2>

			<p>
				Now we're building and refining the tools, patterns, and systems that will remain beyond my
				tenure. I'm mentoring other devs on accessibility, performance and responsive design. I'm
				leading conversations that examine our processes and productivity, identifying ways we can
				continue to improve.
			</p>

			<p>
				Success isn't measured in 'what Mike did,' rather it's how the team has gotten better since
				Mike arrived.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section>
			<h2>What I'm looking for</h2>

			<p>
				I'm seeking an environment where design and engineering respect and collaborate closely with
				each other. I want to join a team that embraces reflection and optimization. I want to be
				part of a company who knows that supporting their employees will lead to greater efficiency
				and delighted users.
			</p>

			<p>
				If I sound like the type of teammate you're looking for, let's talk. You can contact me via
				the social links above or <a href=`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`>reach out</a>.
			</p>
		</section>
	</section>
</Layout>
